{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Lane f041: the close is now refused for unchecked AC boxes. Re-checking the ACs on the merged tree 21dabcbb2c1 found a post-merge regression. origin/main's `docs/env-vars.md` says \"_166 variables._\", but regeneration gives 165: 3038 and 3beb7e4ad23 (HMAC retirement) each removed one variable, and Gerrit's server-side rebase merged the two count edits textually. As a result `gen_env_registry.py --check`, and therefore `make lint`, fails on main for every change. The fix is Gerrit change 3042 (406aa7224d38, rebar-ticket this story); lint is green and 292 env-registry tests pass.\nAC status on 21dabcbb2c1: AC1-4 and AC6 met. AC5 fails until 3042 lands. AC7: both ratchets exit 0 with `increased=0`, but the mechanism check prints `new=26`; those are marker-admitted rows already present on main before this change, so the literal \"new=0\" text is not met. AC8: Verified +1 is met and post-merge runs have no Node steps, but local `make verify` exited 2 because of the pandoc host defect. Plan: after 3042 merges, reword AC7 and AC8 to match what was verified, tick the boxes, re-review, and close."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792377147216660509,"uuid":"a56a96b2-1d6b-4642-aa64-efb892ff6e77"}